From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: shell32: the folder view follows its folder

A file another program made, changed or deleted in the folder File Explorer
showed (a download, a program saving there, a Linux program, a file on a
share) did not appear or go until the folder was opened again: the shell's
change notices reach only the process that sends them. As Windows' File
Explorer watches the folder it shows, the view now waits on the folder's
changes (FindFirstChangeNotification) on a thread of its own and, a moment
after they stop, reads the folder again: it adds what is new, drops what is
gone and takes the new size and date of what changed -- the selection and
the scroll position stay.

Gate: make test-folderwatch.
